<p>This page explains how AI tools assisted with compiling and organizing the SR-177 Weber County analysis. The site should be treated as a structured research aid, not an official source or legal, financial, engineering, or real-estate advice.</p>

<div class="section-label jump-target" id="what-ai-helped-with">What AI Helped With</div>
<h2>Compilation and Organization</h2>

<p>AI tools helped draft, organize, summarize, and review site content from collected research materials and cited public sources. AI assistance was also used to improve page structure, navigation labels, source grouping, and reader-facing explanations.</p>

<p>AI tools did not create official project records, alignment maps, right-of-way boundaries, funding commitments, legal determinations, or parcel-specific conclusions.</p>

<div class="section-label jump-target" id="human-review">Human Review</div>
<h2>Editorial Review</h2>

<p>Content changes are reviewed before publication for clarity, source support, and consistency with the site's editorial rules. The review process prioritizes conservative wording when UDOT, city, county, state, or regional planning records do not support a stronger claim.</p>

<div class="section-label jump-target" id="verification-limits">Verification Limits</div>
<h2>What Readers Should Not Assume</h2>

<div class="callout warning">
  <p><strong>Important limit:</strong> Nothing on this site confirms whether a specific parcel will be acquired, whether a final alignment has been selected, or whether construction funding has been allocated. Those determinations must come from official UDOT, local government, county, court, legislative, or recorded property sources.</p>
</div>

<p>AI-assisted summaries can contain mistakes, omit context, or overstate the significance of a source. For any important decision, readers should verify the cited source and consult qualified professionals where appropriate.</p>

<div class="section-label jump-target" id="source-policy">Source Policy</div>
<h2>How Claims Should Be Checked</h2>

<p>Factual claims should point back to the site's cited references whenever possible. The <a href="references.html">References &amp; Sources</a> page is the starting point for checking official UDOT materials, Wasatch Front Regional Council planning documents, city records, county records, media reports, and legal or technical references.</p>

<p>The <a href="whats-changed.html">What's Changed</a> page records substantive content, source, guidance, and page-structure updates so readers can see when the site has changed.</p>

<div class="section-label jump-target" id="reader-guidance">Reader Guidance</div>
<h2>How to Use This Site Safely</h2>

<ul>
  <li>Use the site to understand topics, timelines, and questions to ask.</li>
  <li>Use official sources for final decisions about property, legal rights, project status, and public comment deadlines.</li>
  <li>Verify parcel-specific questions with UDOT, Weber County, local governments, recorded property documents, and qualified professional advice.</li>
  <li>Report source problems or stale information so the site can be corrected.</li>
</ul>